class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Type in the missing words. </span><span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>"}]}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le07ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le07ob07re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le07ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le07ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Hey Pete. Are you still having trouble with your new phone?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Don't talk to me about that! I'm really upset right now. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: What's going on? Are you still getting that crackling sound?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: No, that's fine. The phone just keeps dying out of the blue. I can't do anything about it. The worst part is that I'm expecting a couple of important calls later! The dinner is at 7 tonight.", "id": 1}, {"time": "20500", "image": "engenn6le07ob07re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Aha, I see. Well, this is what you get when you buy a cool smartphone. They always stop working at some point!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I think you're right. Wait, I've got to run. The battery is almost dead!", "id": 2}, {"time": "34500", "image": "engenn6le07ob07re2img06.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Can you talk now? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm not sure anymore! It says battery fully charged but it means nothing to me!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Robert</span>: Well, I guess it's good to be old-school sometimes. I'm very happy with my flip phone. I can talk for hours on this thing! </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Maybe I'll buy one next time. Ok, I've got to run. I'm going to charge the battery. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: Sure thing. I'll talk to you later! </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Take care, man.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Goes on a Blind Date"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Talk to You Later"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le07ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Closing Phone Conversations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "It's important to use expressions to close a phone conversation. You use polite expressions with people you don't know. </br>You can use more informal expressions with your friends or family."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Whenever you are talking on the phone, it can be difficult for a few reasons:  <ol><li>You are not able to see the other person you are speaking with. </li><li>You are not able to see how he or she is reacting to your conversation.</li></ol>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Informal Conversation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Polite Conversation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Talk to you soon.</br> I've got to run.</br> Bye.</br> Take care.</br> I'd better get going!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's been nice talking to you.</br> Good bye.</br> Thank you for calling.</br> I'll talk with you soon.</br> I will call you back ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I've got to run. Talk to you later.</br> <span class=\"strong\">Ted</span>: Sure thing. Take care, man."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Future Actions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.</li> <li>When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">going to</span>.</li> <li>When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.</li> <li>When you talk about schedules or timetables in the future, you use the Simple Present tense.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verb Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Maybe I'll buy one next time.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm going to charge the battery again.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm expecting a couple of important calls this evening.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present tense</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The dinner is at 7 tonight.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "smartphone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cell phone that connects to the Internet and takes pictures"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My smartphone stopped working!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about cell phones."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "battery "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the part of a device that provides energy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The battery is almost dead."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "charged"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "full of energy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The battery is fully charged."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flip phone"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an older model of cell phone that you can flip open"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I can talk for hours with my flip phone."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "old school"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not trendy; out of fashion"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's good to be old school sometimes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to die"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to stop working"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My phone keeps dying out of the blue."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le07ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Role play 3 different phone conversations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For each conversation, make sure you use expressions to end them properly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be sure to be polite and friendly."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles with your partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I role play a telephone conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about technology and gadgets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I want to do in the future."}]}]}